meta {
  name: review condition
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/admin/standards/versions/{{standardVersionId}}/conditions/review
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "requirementId": "{{requirementId}}",
    "conditionText": "",
    "reviewedRole": "CONDITIONAL_OBLIGATION",
    "reviewStatus": "CONFIRMED",
    "authoriseExclusion": false,
    "reviewerNotes": "Validated via Bruno"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: any [200, 400, 404, 409]
}

docs {
  Records a condition decision. WRITES. STANDARDS_ADMIN or ADMIN.

  conditionText must match a condition on that requirement VERBATIM — copy it from the GET above. A
  typo returns 404 rather than creating an override that matches nothing and sits in the list
  looking authoritative.

  reviewerNotes is REQUIRED: a role change with no rationale is unreviewable later. 400 if blank.

  THE GUARD WORTH TESTING: set reviewedRole SCOPE_GATE with authoriseExclusion true, confirm the
  response shows canDriveNotApplicable true — then re-post with CONDITIONAL_OBLIGATION and
  authoriseExclusion still true. It must come back FALSE. Exclusion authority is recomputed every
  revision, never carried over, or a requirement would stay excluded on a classification that no
  longer exists.

  Not supplied by the caller, by design: the actor comes from the session, and the requirement set
  is resolved server-side. An author a caller could set is not an audit trail.
}
